                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "We really don't need the actual output of the command in the commit message.  The point is that the tests can be reproduced by others, and you've documented the tests you've personally ran to make sure you're not pushing testing work on others.  The actual output might be interesting sometimes if we're trying to document a change, but \"output didn't change\" is perfectly adequate.\n\n+1 on needing a tested statement."
